+   "suggested_fix": "Either make the limiter module-level (one pool shared by every useMetaprojectTree instance in the webview, with MAX_TREE_READS as the process budget), and correct the MAX_TREE_READS comment so it says the permits are shared by all windows. Or treat a permit refusal (`unavailable` whose message starts with 'Too many Metaproject reads') as retryable once or twice, with a short jittered backoff inside `read`, before the folder is marked failed. The second covers both the tree and cross-window pressure. Premise judge note: each Tauri window has its own JS context, so a module-level pool does not cover several windows; implement the retry option (retry an `unavailable` permit refusal once or twice with a short jittered delay before marking the folder failed) and correct the MAX_TREE_READS comment so it does not claim one window owns all 8 permits."
+  },
