+   "severity": "minor",
+   "file": "apps/desktop/src/metaproject/useMetaprojectTree.ts",
+   "problem": "Nielsen #9 (error recovery) and #5 (error prevention). When a tree read answers stale-snapshot, the catch calls onStale, which shows the explorer's 'Refresh catalog' banner, and then falls through to the generic failure branch. The folder (or its Show more row) becomes 'Could not load. Project knowledge changed while loading.' with a Retry button. Retry re-sends the same retired snapshot: `read` pins `expectedSnapshotId: state.current[scope].snapshot`, and a page Retry re-sends the old cursor. The CLI therefore answers stale-snapshot again. In this delta the transport (platform/metaproject.ts) newly turns any answer for another snapshot into this error, which makes the path reachable from a second source. The delta's own Load-more search fix (MetaprojectView.loadMoreSearch) handles the same error by showing only the banner, so the two paths disagree.",
+   "suggested_fix": "In the catch, after `latest.current.onStale()`, return without marking the folder failed. Leave the folder in its loading state (or drop it, as the not-found branch does), because Refresh catalog changes the snapshot and the tree then re-reads it anyway. This matches loadMoreSearch, which sets snapshotMismatch and no inline error. Extend the existing MetaprojectView test 'a tree answer for another snapshot, or a stale-snapshot refusal, shows the stale banner and none of its rows' to assert that no treeitem reads 'Could not load.' while the banner shows. Operator decision (round 1 fix round): a stale snapshot shows the Refresh catalog banner. Make the tree read consistent with loadMoreSearch: after onStale(), do not mark the folder failed (no dead Retry row); assert in a view test that no 'Could not load.' row shows while the banner does."
+  },
+  {
+   "id": "r2-testing-practices-w2-F1",
+   "severity": "minor",
+   "file": "apps/desktop/src/metaproject/MetaprojectTree.tsx",
+   "problem": "Fix round 1 (frontend-w1-F-001 / ui-ux-w1-UX-001) added two mechanisms so that focus is never taken from outside the tree. The first is the `onBlur` microtask that forgets the focused row when focus moves out. The second is the `active` guard in the layout effect. No test drives the case they exist for: a tree row holds focus, focus then moves outside, and only after that does the focused row leave (Show more's last page arrives, or a loading or error row turns into children). Every test that focuses `outside` keeps it outside without ever focusing a row first, or leaves the focused row in place: 'data arriving never moves focus' (a mouse click on the chevron, so no row was ever focused), the reveal test and the Home/End test (the rows stay). The two keyboard tests (Retry, Show more) keep focus inside the tree.",
+   "suggested_fix": "In MetaprojectTree.dom.test.tsx, add a test. Hold `|next`. Focus the Show more row and press Enter, so the row is focused and loading. Focus an `outside` button inside act(). Release `|next`. Assert that `document.activeElement === outside`, that the appended rows are present (positive artifact) and that 'Show more' is gone. Add a twin with a held folder read, where the focused loading row is replaced by children."
